WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.050
Being the nicest person on the team

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.250
cost him the promotion.

3
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:04.750
His boss explained why

4
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:05.650
in one sentence.

5
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.750
He said yes to every request,

6
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.850
even at 9 p.m. on a Friday.

7
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.250
His laptop sat open on the couch

8
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.750
while his dinner went cold.

9
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.250
Coworkers called him "reliable,"

10
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.450
but nobody ever asked

11
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.350
what he wanted.

12
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:18.550
His boss said,

13
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.750
"I can't promote someone

14
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:20.950
I've never heard disagree."

15
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.950
In year one, he took on 6 extra projects

16
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.150
without asking for credit.

17
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.250
In year two, a new hire

18
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.150
with louder opinions

19
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.350
got his best client.

20
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.750
In year three, he trained the person

21
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.250
who then became his manager.

22
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.650
In year four, he said "no" once,

23
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.450
and his boss finally leaned in.

24
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:38.650
Agreeing with everyone

25
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.150
makes you easy to like

26
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.350
and easy to overlook.

27
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.150
Try this once this week:

28
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.350
"I see it differently.

29
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:45.550
Here's why."

30
00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:46.750
I'm Dimples.

31
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.150
I talk about the things we feel

32
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.650
but never say out loud.

33
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:51.850
Follow for more.
